# Machine-written sidecars beside the change-sets. The DATED change-set files
# (changesets/inbox_actions/<date>.json) are the audit trail of what was
# proposed and applied and ARE committed; these two are regenerated on every
# run and carry only the last result, so a commit of one is noise that reads
# like a hand-authored decision.
changesets/inbox_actions/last_placement.json
changesets/inbox_actions/last_canary.json
changesets/inbox_actions/last_canary_*.json

# Dead Modal handler carrying four hard-coded live credentials (an Instantly
# API key, a GitHub token, a Slack webhook URL and a Google service-account
# private key). Nothing imports or deploys it: execution/webhooks.json maps
# only lead_sync, to execution/modal_lead_sync.py, so ignoring it breaks no
# deploy path. It is already deleted in the working tree.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE LINE BELOW: git ignores nothing it is already
# tracking, and this file IS tracked at HEAD and in three commits. The entry
# only stops a future copy from being added. Rotating the four credentials and
# untracking the file (git rm --cached) are Lorenzo's calls:
# runbooks/GO_LIVE_CHECKLIST.md step 0 and runbooks/DECISIONS_FOR_LORENZO.md 0.1.
execution/modal_reply_handler_v2.py

# Lead manifests of the 2026-09-25 deliverability change-set: one row per
# parked lead with name, email and company (PII). The root .gitignore
# un-ignores changesets/**/*.json, so the folder is excluded here as a whole.
changesets/deliverability_2026_09_25/manifests/
